    2. Generate M segment rows of width W with random black/red content
    3. Choose grid height H >= M+3 and grid width GW >= W+2
    4. Scatter M marker rows among H rows (gaps 1-3, at least 1 non-marker row exists)
    5. For each marker row, pick blue_col so that blue_col+1+W <= GW-1, set teal_col = blue_col+1+W
    6. Fill marker row outside the bracket span with random black/red
    7. Fill all non-marker rows with random black/red
    8. Output = vertically stacked segments in row order
